      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 916533872,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This should not usually happen, because the hierarchy stats only look at first level children of the root tree (which itself may be wrong for dissectors that put protocols as children of other protocols?), but there's some interesting interactions with faked items and dissectors that call `proto_item_get_parent[_nth]` or `proto_tree_get_parent_tree` and add items onto the result. Because of the faked items, those functions can get back up to the root tree.",
